<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.9.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01403</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.9.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6782bc5e-419b-456e-b877-b41eed38a66f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will study exponential functions and their graphs in context. Given a graph or a description of a relationship, you write one quantity as a function of another and then use the function to answer questions about the context. You will also produce graphs of exponential functions, paying close attention to the appropriate domain and range.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Analyze a situation and determine whether it makes sense to connect the points on the graph that represents the situation.</item>
  <item>Describe the relationship in a graph of an exponential function using function notation.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>5.9.1: Evaluating Expressions for Different Values of \(x\)</item>
  <item>5.9.2: Analyze Underlying Relationship in a Graph of a Function  <list id="list-00003">
    <item> 5.9.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 5.9.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
 
  <item>5.9.3: Graph Equations to Solve Problem <list id="list-00004">
    <item> 5.9.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 5.9.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>s</item>
 
  <item>5.9.4: Deciding on Graphing Window</item>
  <item>5.9.5: Interpret Graphs to Find Approximate Values</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>5.9.6: Practice</item>
  <item>5.9.7: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
